.TH CHTTPSVR_RESP_PRINTF 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_resp_printf \- format and append a printf-style string to the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_resp_printf(chttpsvr_resp *resp,
                                    const char *format, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Formats format and the variadic arguments using printf semantics and
appends the result to the response body, equivalent to formatting into
a temporary string and passing it to chttpsvr_resp_write_str.  A small
internal stack buffer is used for short output; longer output falls
back to a temporary heap allocation (freed before the function
returns) sized exactly to the formatted length.  Multiple calls
accumulate into the response body just like chttpsvr_resp_write_str.

The format string is checked at compile time with GCC's
__attribute__((format(printf, 2, 3))).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - Formatted output appended to the body.
ccol_invalid_args      - resp or format is NULL, or the underlying
                          vsnprintf call reports an encoding error.
ccol_not_enough_memory - The body buffer or the temporary heap
                          fallback buffer could not be allocated.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_str (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_json (3)
